Your task is to build a music play app that downloads audio files from a
user-configured S3 compatable bucket (e.g. AWS or Backblaze) and plays them
locally on an iOS device.

The app will be built with flutter.
I do not have a MAC: all development must happen on this linux machine.
I would like to test the app on my ios phone, you will need to guide me through
the process of deploying the app to my ios phone for testing.

Responsiveness is a top priority in terms of the user experience.
I will be using a very large audio database, so this should be considered when
writing the code.
Each audio file will have an embedded thumbnail image which should be extracted
and cached as necessary. I want the thumbnail image to be displayed with songs
and albums. The thumbnail image may not necessarily be square.

An SQLite database will be used to cache audio file metadata.
Carefully write the code to ensure that the metadata in the database is
always consistent with what songs have been downloaded into the filesystem.

Downloading from the S3 compatable bucket should happen incrementally.
E.g. if the remote has only one file added, we should not be downloading the
entire database again.
It is possible that a song on the remote is modified (e.g. its metadata changed),
in this case we should re-download the song and make sure the metadata update
is reflected in the SQLite database.
If files are removed from the remote database they should be removed locally also.
The audio files will be synced from the remote only when the user requests for
a sync to take place (no automatic download).
We should only pull from the bucket, we should NEVER push or write to the remote bucket.

For the S3 remote the user provides: bucket name, region, access key ID, secret access key.

Be carefull to properly handle all possible errors, prefering to show the
user an error message over silently crashing or showing a blank screen.

# Library Page

When the app opens it should bring you to the "library" page in which the user
can browse songs and add them to the play queue.

There should be three "tabs" at the top: "Artists", "Albums" and "Songs".
Swiping left/right should smoothly change between the three tabs.

On the top of each tab there should be a search bar for searching the
Artist/Albums/Songs and a "sort-by" dropdown.
The artist tab dropdown should be able to sort by:
  - artist name A-Z
  - number of songs
  - number of albums
  - most recently updated (the most recent file created timestamp of all of the artist songs as fetched from the remote)
The album tab dropdown should be able to sort by:
  - album name A-Z
  - by artist (A-Z)
  - by song count
  - most recently updated (calculated in same way as artist most recently updated)
The song tab dropdown should be able to sort by:
  - Song name A-Z
  - By artist then album (A-Z)
  - Most recently added (calculated in same way as other recently added)
Notice that when calculating "most recent" I care about the file creation time,
not the file update time (e.g. updating metadata should not bump the track).

## Artists Tab

Should show a sorted list of artist entries.


## Albums tab

Show sorted list of album entries. Each entry should show number of songs,
artist name, album name and show album art, and total runtime of album.
Pressing an album should bring you to the album page.

## Songs tab

Should show a list of song entries.

## Artist Page

The artist page should show the title of the artist, the number songs and albums
this artist is associated with,
the total runtime of all songs by the artist,
then list the albums this artist is a part of in a left/right scrollable list with album art
then list the artists songs.
There should be a button for "play songs" and a buttong for "add songs to queue".
Each album in this list should show the number of tracks and name.
If the artist is not part of any album then just dont have any albums scrollable at all.
Pressing an album should bring you to that album page.
Below the albums scrollable there should be a list of songs by the artist grouped
by album and in alphabetical order.
The list of albums should use the same "album entry" element as in the albums
tab of the library page (code reuse).
Next to each song the duration of the song should be shown.
This list of songs should use the same "song entry" element as the songs
tab (code reuse).

## Album Page

The album page should show the album title, number of tracks, total runtime,
album art, artist name.

There should be a button for "play songs" and a buttong for "add songs to queue".

Then list all sogns in the album using a list of "song entries".
The same song entries as in the song tab of the library page (code reuse).

## Song Entry

This element is used in a number pages and works the same everywhere.
It is a rectangle shape spanning the width and with a fixed vertical height.
It shows the information for a single song to be used in a vertically scrollable list.
The entry should show the song name, artist, (album if applicable), duration,
thumbnail image.
The entries should be vertically compact.
Get song names from audio file metadata (cached from the database), not audio file name.

Pressing a songs entry should "play now" the song.

## Artist Entry

This tab should list all artists that have been found in the audio metadata.
It should be a scrollable list.
Under the artist name, each entry should show
the number of albums and the number of songs this artist has been a part of.

# Song Queue

Playing of songs works by adding songs to a queue.
Long-pressing an album/artist/song entry should bring up a small menu element above where
the user long-pressed which should have options for "play now" and "add to queue"
and "play next".
A long press is 100ms.
"Play now" means replace the current play queue with this.
"Add to queue means append to the end of the play queue."
"Play next" means insert these songs into the play queue immediatly after the
current playing song.

The current playing songs should be shown at the bottom of the screen
(above all pages) in a small transulcent rectangular box with the song thumbnail
on the left, the song name, artist name, album name, total duration and current duration through the
song with a thin progress bar showing current progress through the song at the
bottom of the rectangle.
On the left there should be buttons for "start of song / prev song", "pause/play"
and "next songs" in the normal conventional symbols for these actions.
This rectangle should also show then number of songs in the queue and the
total queue duration and current progress time at the top clearly distinct from the current playing song.
This "song queue info box" should look similar to the one on the VLC app except
I have a bit more info.

If the user clicks or swipes up on the "song queue info box", then the song
queue page will come up from the bottom of the screen and stop when the song
queue info box gets to the top of the screen.
The queue page can be closed again by swiping down from the song queue info
box.
The queue page should show the list of songs in the queue, the user should be
able to rearrange songs in the queue by dragging them up/down. And the user
should be able to remove songs from the queue by swiping them to the left.
It should clearly show which song in the queue is currently playing.

Currently playing song should be shown in my ios notifications page, with
album art and play/pause next/prev buttongs.

# Settings Page

The top right of the library page should have a settings button which when clicked
brings you to the setting page.
This page lets you specify the S3 endpoing by letting the user choose
the endpoing url, bucket name, region, access key id, secret access key.
The secret access key should be in hidden password dots by default but there should
be an "eye" button in the left of the text box to show/hide the password.

There should be a button to save the configuration when updated (it should indicate if you
have unsaved changes).
Below these remote settings there should be a button to "sync now" which
will scan the remote for new/changed songs, download them and update the
appropriate metadata.
The download shoud show the current progress.

If an error occurs during download, make sure to properly handle this and show
the user a usefull error message that can be used to diagnose.

A wide variety of audio files should be supported for playing and extracting
metadata including: mp3, flac, opus.

There should be a button to load the the test remote settings which are:
{
  bucket: 'music-test-7b22',
  region: 'eu-central-003',
  endpoint: 's3.eu-central-003.backblazeb2.com',
  accessKeyId: '0038a8d5945ebb5000000000d',
  secretAccessKey: 'K003/JysvhgF0AqOgOVnztwDy39SrIU',
}

Note that some songs in my database have no Album associated with them.
This is ok and expected, that means they are just not part of any album and
you dont need to create any kind of "unknown album" album entry.

# Style Guidelines

I want a minimal clean and consistent application style.
Simple minimalistic icons should be used.
Use system fonts and be consistent.
- Prefer **anchored, inline popover menus** near the user's touch target for sort/context actions.
- Avoid bottom-sheet/action-sheet style menus for routine in-page actions when an anchored popover is feasible.
- Keep control buttons visually simple: minimal borders/fills, consistent hit targets, and no mixed icon styles in the same row.
Make sure the app is responsive even when handling large music databases.
